Windows Registry Editor Version 5.00

; Chrome Enterprise Core (a.k.a. Chrome Browser Cloud Management, CBCM) enrollment token.
; The official alternative to fake-mdm.reg: real cloud management makes the device TRUSTED,
; so off-store ExtensionSettings / ExtensionInstallForcelist entries are honored instead of
; rewritten to [BLOCKED]. Unlike fake-mdm.reg this is NOT the Windows MDM signal, so it is
; not gated by SUITE_HOME and works on Windows Home too.
;
; 1. In the Google Admin console (admin.google.com) — a free Chrome Enterprise Core account
;    with a verified domain — go to Devices > Chrome > Managed browsers > Enroll, and copy
;    the enrollment token (looks like a GUID).
; 2. Paste it below, replacing PASTE_YOUR_ENROLLMENT_TOKEN_HERE.
; 3. Run elevated (writes HKLM), then restart Chrome.
; 4. 32-bit Chrome? Also add the same value under ...\WOW6432Node\Policies\Google\Chrome.
;
; VERIFY: chrome://policy shows the machine enrolled (Chrome Enterprise Core) and
;   chrome://management reports the browser is managed. Then apply chrome.reg (or push the
;   force-install from the Admin console) — no fake-mdm.reg needed.

[HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\SOFTWARE\Policies\Google\Chrome]
"CloudManagementEnrollmentToken"="PASTE_YOUR_ENROLLMENT_TOKEN_HERE"
